nd type(s) for *: 'NoneType' and 'int'\n```\n\nTrack down why this happens and fix it so the program runs cleanly. When it\nworks, `python3 main.py` should print exactly:\n\n```\nTotal: 5.0\n```\n\nDone when `python3 main.py` exits successfully and prints that line.\n"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "stdout", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "without", "fresh_subagents": 1, "harness": "opencode", "harness_version": "0.0.0--202610170355 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/opencode-src/bin/64e2bf8bf00eca1c6ad4486e29eb84f7907d1d35/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: task]\n[tool: task]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nThe script runs cleanly now: `python3 main.py` prints `Total: 5.0` and exits with code 0.\n\n**What the subagent found (first call):** `rate` becomes `None` at `app/pricing.py:8`, where `get_rate()` does `return SETTINGS.get(\"rate\")`. There's no `\"rate\"` key in the settings, so `.get()` quietly returns `None`. The crash only shows up later, at `app/report.py:9` (`rate * count`).\n\n**Missing settings key (second call, same subagent session):** the code expects `\"rate\"`, but `settings.json:2` spells it `\"rat\"`.\n\n**Fix:** I renamed the key from `\"rat\"` to `\"rate\"` in `settings.json`.\n\n`get_rate()` still uses `.get()` with no default, so a missing key would fail the same confusing way again. If you want it to fail at the source instead, it could use `SETTINGS[\"rate\"]`, which raises a `KeyError` right away.", "paced_wait_s":